%[text] # Getting Started with the Loudspeaker System Toolbox
%[text] **J.G. Vermond, JVsound**
%%
%[text] ## Introduction
%[text] This toolbox models loudspeaker systems in the frequency domain: a driver (`comp.Driver`) mounted in an enclosure (a subclass of `comp.Enclosure`), combined into a loudspeaker system (`lspsys`) that calculates the response of the system as a `result` object.
%%
%[text] ## Build the loudspeaker system
%[text] Create an `lspsys` object:
sys = lspsys;
%%
%[text] ## Add an enclosure
%[text] Give the system a closed box of 200 L:
sys.Enclosure = comp.ClosedBox;
sys.Enclosure.RearVolume = 200e-3;
%%
%[text] ## Add a driver
%[text] Mount a `comp.Driver` in the enclosure and set its Thiele-Small parameters, here of a B&C 21SW152-8:
sys.Enclosure.Driver = comp.Driver;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Re = 6;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Le = 2.2e-3;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Qes = 0.38;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Qms = 6.4;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Fs = 32;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Sd = 1680e-4;
sys.Enclosure.Driver.Vas = 200e-3;
%%
%[text] ## Solve and plot
%[text] `createResult` solves the system and returns the response as a `result` object. Plot the sound pressure level at 1 m for 2.83 V:
res = sys.createResult;
semilogx(res.Frequency,res.SoundPressureLevel,LineWidth=1.5) %[output:43bc74b1]
grid on %[output:43bc74b1]
xlabel("Frequency [Hz]") %[output:43bc74b1]
ylabel("Sound pressure level [dB]") %[output:43bc74b1]
title("Sound pressure level of the loudspeaker system") %[output:43bc74b1]
%%
%[text] ## Next steps
%[text] - [Documentation overview](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','overview.m'))) — links to the documentation of every class and to the list of symbols.
%[text] - [`closedBoxExample`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'examples','closedBoxExample.m'))) — a closed box: impedance, sound pressure level and the effect of the box volume.
%[text] - [`feaEnclosureExample`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'examples','feaEnclosureExample.m'))) — a front-loaded horn from the results of an FEA model, with the maximum sound pressure level.
%[text] - [`result`](matlab:open(fullfile(fileparts(fileparts(which('lspsys'))),'doc','result','resultdoc.m'))) — what the results hold, including `splMax`. \

